WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:15.228
Unit twenty: Volunteering at School. Today you will tell a story about helping with the past simple.

4
00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:18.366
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.649
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.647
Volunteer.

7
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.555
Volunteer means to work without pay to help others.

8
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.347
We volunteered at the school library.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.509
Your turn. Say: Volunteer.

10
00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.507
Volunteer.

11
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:39.903
Help.

12
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:43.276
Help means to make things easier for someone.

13
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:45.686
We helped younger students read.

14
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.831
Your turn. Say: Help.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.378
Help.

16
00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:53.920
Event.

17
00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:57.288
Event means something planned that happens.

18
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.987
The school event was a big success.

19
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:02.887
Your turn. Say: Event.

20
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:06.676
Event.

21
00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.383
Organize.

22
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:12.056
Organize means to plan and arrange something.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.626
We organized a clean-up day.

24
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.695
Your turn. Say: Organize.

25
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:21.651
Organize.

26
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:23.093
Team.

27
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.060
Team means a group working together.

28
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.452
Our team had five members.

29
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.389
Your turn. Say: Team.

30
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:35.037
Team.

31
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:36.773
Community.

32
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:40.781
Community means the people who live in one area.

33
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:43.511
The library is for the whole community.

34
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:46.711
Your turn. Say: Community.

35
00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:50.510
Community.

36
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.089
Donate.

37
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:55.733
Donate means to give money or things to help others.

38
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:58.618
We donated books to a village school.

39
00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:02.357
Your turn. Say: Donate.

40
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:05.992
Donate.

41
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.577
Proud.

42
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:10.873
Proud means happy about something good you did.

43
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:13.123
I felt proud of our work.

44
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.148
Your turn. Say: Proud.

45
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.862
Proud.

46
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:24.538
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:27.905
Visal, what did your class do last month?

48
00:02:29.017 --> 00:02:31.899
We decided to volunteer at the school event.

49
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:34.518
What did you organize?

50
00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:40.278
We organized a book sale. My team collected over two hundred books!

51
00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:42.721
What happened to the money?

52
00:02:43.817 --> 00:02:48.605
We donated it to the community library. We all felt proud.

53
00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.418
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:55.734
Grammar focus: Past simple (decided, organized).

55
00:02:56.034 --> 00:02:57.175
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:57.883 --> 00:02:59.848
We organized a book sale.

57
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.610
We donated the money last month.

58
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.423
Our class decided to help.

59
00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:13.071
Regular verbs add -ed. If the verb ends in -e, just add -d: decide → decided.

60
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:18.060
Be careful! Don't say: We organize a book sale last month.

61
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.719
Say: We organized a book sale last month.

62
00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:26.296
Use the past simple, with -ed, for finished actions.

63
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.938
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:30.733 --> 00:03:31.816
Our Book Sale.

65
00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:35.706
Last month, our class decided to volunteer at the school event.

66
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.106
We organized a book sale as a team.

67
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.131
Students and teachers donated old books, and we sold them cheaply.

68
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:48.155
We raised money and donated it to the community library.

69
00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.420
We felt proud to help, and we learned the value of teamwork.

70
00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:57.280
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:58.117 --> 00:04:00.186
Last week, we blank a book sale.

72
00:04:00.486 --> 00:04:04.569
A, organized. B, organize. C, organizing.

73
00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.191
The answer is A: organized.

74
00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.139
To give money or things to help others is to blank.

75
00:04:14.439 --> 00:04:18.870
A, donate. B, volunteer. C, decide.

76
00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:24.201
The answer is A: donate.

77
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.524
Happy about something good you did is blank.

78
00:04:27.824 --> 00:04:31.152
A, proud. B, tired. C, worried.

79
00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.386
The answer is A: proud.

80
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.694
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.944
How could students help their school community?

82
00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.215
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:54.515 --> 00:05:04.505
Students could clean the school garden or help younger children read. Last year, my class painted our classroom, and we felt very proud.

84
00:05:04.805 --> 00:05:06.515
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:07.417 --> 00:05:12.437
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple (decided, organized).

86
00:05:12.737 --> 00:05:16.818
Today's value is helping others. Give your time to help people in need.

87
00:05:17.118 --> 00:05:20.130
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

88
00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.082
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

